WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.972
There was much to prepare before the voyage.

2
00:00:03.973 --> 00:00:06.049
First, they needed a boat.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:11.035
A local fisherman named Joe had a boat for sale.

4
00:00:11.036 --> 00:00:14.145
Dr. Dolittle and Tommy looked over the boat.

5
00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:16.541
It was named The Curlew.

6
00:00:16.542 --> 00:00:19.779
The Curlew would be perfect for their journey.

7
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.863
However, there was one problem.

8
00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:28.126
"You need three people to sail this vessel," Joe explained.

9
00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:32.109
"Will you hire two sailors?" Tommy asked the doctor.

10
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.584
Dr. Dolittle shook his head.

11
00:00:34.585 --> 00:00:37.854
"No, I always prefer to sail with friends."

12
00:00:37.855 --> 00:00:42.470
"What about Matthew?" Tommy suggested.

13
00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:46.225
"It may be a difficult journey," Dr. Dolittle stated.

14
00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:48.698
"I think Matthew may be too old."

15
00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:52.365
"Then how about Luke?" Tommy said excitedly.

16
00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:54.608
The doctor stopped in his tracks.

17
00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.464
"Yes, that sounds like a good idea, Tommy," he said.

18
00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:01.410
"Let’s go,

19
00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:04.250
Jip." Luke lived just outside of

20
00:01:04.251 --> 00:01:06.875
Puddleby. Most everyone was afraid of

21
00:01:06.876 --> 00:01:10.922
Luke. He didn’t talk much, nor was he friendly to

22
00:01:10.923 --> 00:01:16.615
others. But Dr. Dolittle and Tommy both knew he had a good

23
00:01:16.616 --> 00:01:21.523
heart. "That’s odd," said Dr. Dolittle when they reached Luke’s

24
00:01:21.524 --> 00:01:29.489
cottage. "Luke is usually sitting over there"—he pointed to a rocking chair—"and Bob always comes over to greet us."

25
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.915
Bob was Luke’s big black scary dog.

26
00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:36.020
He growled and barked at everyone.

27
00:01:36.021 --> 00:01:38.622
But he didn’t mind the doctor and Tommy.

28
00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:41.917
And he was friendly with Jip, too.

29
00:01:41.918 --> 00:01:44.050
Tommy looked through the window.

30
00:01:44.051 --> 00:01:46.920
"There’s nobody inside," he remarked.

31
00:01:46.921 --> 00:01:49.777
It was very strange indeed.

32
00:01:49.778 --> 00:01:52.725
Jip kept his nose close to the ground.

33
00:01:52.726 --> 00:01:59.736
Suddenly he let out a low growl.

34
00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:02.386
"What is it, Jip?" asked the doctor.

35
00:02:02.387 --> 00:02:05.953
Jip lifted his head and let out a pitiful howl.

36
00:02:05.954 --> 00:02:08.000
He was clearly upset.

37
00:02:08.001 --> 00:02:11.594
Dr. Dolittle kept asking him what the matter was.

38
00:02:11.595 --> 00:02:15.816
But Jip only howled more loudly.

39
00:02:15.817 --> 00:02:20.462
Finally Jip said to the doctor, "I have to go quickly!"

40
00:02:20.463 --> 00:02:24.717
"Jip, what on earth is happening?" Dr. Dolittle shouted.

41
00:02:24.718 --> 00:02:28.089
"I don’t have time to explain," he barked.

42
00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.468
And with that Jip quickly ran off.

43
00:02:32.469 --> 00:02:34.919
They returned home without Jip.

44
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.590
"Is Jip back yet?"

45
00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:39.762
Dr. Dolittle asked when he walked in the door.

46
00:02:39.764 --> 00:02:44.180
"We thought he was with you," Dab-Dab said, confused.

47
00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:49.231
"What’s happened, doctor?" Polynesia asked.

48
00:02:49.232 --> 00:02:56.073
Dr. Dolittle told the others about The Curlew, about Luke, and about Jip’s strange behavior."Something

49
00:02:56.074 --> 00:03:00.314
is definitely wrong," the doctor concluded. Suddenly

50
00:03:00.315 --> 00:03:03.696
they heard loud noises outside.

51
00:03:03.697 --> 00:03:05.849
Tommy ran to the window.

52
00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.986
"It’s Jip and . . . Bob!"

53
00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:11.844
The two dogs were very upset.

54
00:03:11.845 --> 00:03:16.374
Bob looked so angry that Tommy felt afraid to get near him.

55
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:20.255
Only Dr. Dolittle was brave enough to approach.

56
00:03:20.256 --> 00:03:24.218
"Jip! Bob! Calm down!" he ordered.

57
00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:25.877
The dogs obeyed.

58
00:03:25.878 --> 00:03:30.741
"Now," continued the doctor, "tell me what happened."

59
00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:32.516
"Luke is a good man.

60
00:03:32.517 --> 00:03:36.727
He didn’t do it," Bob barked over and over again.

61
00:03:36.728 --> 00:03:40.201
"Didn’t do what?" asked Dr. Dolittle.

62
00:03:40.202 --> 00:03:44.792
"He didn’t kill that man!" howled Bob.

63
00:03:44.793 --> 00:03:48.179
Tommy took another step back.

64
00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.306
"Kill who, Bob?" the doctor demanded to know.

65
00:03:52.307 --> 00:03:55.779
"That man fell in the well," wailed Bob.

66
00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.273
"Where is Luke now?" asked Dr. Dolittle.

67
00:03:59.274 --> 00:04:01.845
"In jail," Jip answered.

68
00:04:01.846 --> 00:04:08.220
"We must go and see him," said the doctor, firmly.

